Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6dsp: add the SLIMBUS_7 and SLIMBUS_8 ports

The AFE has eight multi-channel SLIMbus ports, 0x4000 to 0x4011; the
driver knows the first seven pairs. SoCs whose Bluetooth/FM chip
(WCN399x) sits on the LPASS SLIMbus use the last two: SLIMBUS_7_RX/TX
for Bluetooth SCO and A2DP, SLIMBUS_8_TX for the FM receiver (SM6115:
48 kHz, 16 bit, 2 channels).

Add the four ports: their IDs after the last one in the bindings
(149-152), the AFE port map and SLIMbus configuration, the DAIs with
their DAPM widgets, and the routing mixers. The SLIMbus DAIs told TX
from RX by the parity of their ID, which the new IDs do not keep: ask
the DAI for its direction instead.

